10. Engineering Gate PASS, if earned, means only that phase's defined engineering acceptance is satisfied. It is not a release, distribution, license, or unsupported-platform PASS.
11. `docs/gltf-scene-editor-parity-progress.md` is never in a leaf or integration task's initial write set. It may be edited only by a separate ledger task after that phase's integration owner and fresh independent Gate owner explicitly authorize the update.
12. A source implementation task never edits `docs/editor-parity/manifest.json`, `edge-obligations.json`, or acceptance result status merely to make a test or count green.
13. Each independent Gate is source read-only and repair-free. A reviewer reports findings and a binary engineering verdict; it never fixes its own findings.
