## 4. Operational and runtime failure atomicity

### 4.1 Shared-worktree task atomicity

- Leaf tasks add or edit only their exact write sets. Shared wiring files belong exclusively to the phase integration task.
- Leaf code that is not yet wired into production remains inert until integration. A leaf failure therefore cannot partially register an unfinished source into the production target.
- A failed worker stops writing, records final hashes and failing commands, and reports failed. It does not revert anything in the shared worktree.
- An integration task starts only after every dependency worker has stopped and all final hashes match its bound inputs. It performs the only shared CMake/facade/application wiring for that phase.
- If integration fails, it does not update the progress ledger, evidence manifest, or Gate status. The last independently verified phase remains the authoritative engineering baseline. A later repair gets a new scoped task and a new pre-edit binding.
- A Gate failure never causes automatic rollback, cleanup, or self-repair. The coordinator creates a bounded follow-up with a fresh write set.

### 4.2 Product-state atomicity by phase

- P5: validate all fences before side effects; stage CPU state/resources/descriptors; submit with exact queue tokens; publish one immutable renderer/mapping generation; retire superseded resources after dependencies. Pre-submit failure destroys staged resources, post-submit failure retires orphan resources, and active state remains unchanged. `partialPublicationCount` stays zero. Accepted incremental work has zero device-idle calls.
- P6: selection is the sole authority; occurrence mappings are immutable; every accepted pick receives one terminal completion; stale authority/revision/projection/scene/device/viewport/view results have no effect. Old occurrence snapshots outlive or cancel all readbacks that reference them.
- P7: invalid or non-finite math fails before preview mutation. A preview, draw packet, document revision, and renderer delta describe the same accepted state. Overlay replacement uses RHI logical handles and deferred retirement, never native escape hatches or device idle.
- P8: UI emits intents only. `LoadingCandidate`, `Saving/Merging/Compacting`, and `Error` keep the last valid document and render generation visible; the other exact states are `NoDocument`, `ReadyClean`, `ReadyModified`, `GizmoHover`, `GizmoDragging`, and `Modal`. The legacy mutation path is removed only by the integration owner after controller and UI tests are wired.
- P9: Merge and Compact mutate clones only; lifecycle candidates are invisible until document, projection, mapping, GPU generation, selection/history policy, and request epochs are ready for one no-throw publication. Save As stages in the target parent, flushes/closes, publishes immutable resources before the main file, atomically replaces the main file last, and uses a durable recovery journal. Failure preserves active CPU/GPU state, old target, history, selection, path, clean revision, and MRU except explicitly locked invalid-Recent cleanup.
- P10: evidence roots are immutable and identity-bound. Validators run last. A failed, skipped, stale, mixed-SHA, missing-platform, license-blocked, or semantically unmapped result cannot be promoted to PASS. Acceptance execution does not repair source in the same task.

