## 7. APIs, contracts, tests, and acceptance

### 7.1 P5 contracts

`P5-00` freezes a backend-neutral logical transition surface. Exact names may be adjusted only within its write set before downstream tasks start; after `P5-00` completion downstream owners consume it without edits.

Required value surface:

- `StableSceneId { kind, authority, slot, generation }` or an equivalent lossless wrapper over the existing typed IDs.
- `SceneChangeDomain { DocumentMutation, SceneActivation, FullSnapshot }`.
- Eight externally reportable change classes: `Transform`, `MaterialParameters`, `MaterialBinding`, `Light`, `Visibility`, `Hierarchy`, `Topology`, `FullRebuild`.
- `SceneChangeHeader` with schema, authority, base/target document revision, base/target scene epoch, active scene, mutation token/serial, base/target projection digest, and canonical change-set digest.
- Immutable payload ownership; no raw pointer into mutable document/projection data.
- Reason-coded `FullRebuildReason` including scene switch, global Merge, Compact, structural topology, geometry schema, texture schema, mapping mismatch, missed revision, device recovery, unsupported capability, and explicit request.
- Pure CPU `canonicalizeSceneChanges()` with typed validation errors, deterministic serialization/digest, last-write-by-mutation-serial, create/update/delete algebra, parent-before-child derived work, reverse dependency removal, and exact stable-key ordering.

`P5-00` tests:

- shuffled logical input produces identical canonical bytes/digest/order;
- repeated fields coalesce exactly, generation-changing delete/create never collapses;
- invalid authority/kind/revision/payload/hash/range rejects without output;
- empty/duplicate/idempotent cases are explicit;
- public header self-containment and zero backend/native/reference tokens.

`P5-10` implements exact producer and mapping behavior:

- current all-live `changedIds` is never used as a precise delta;
- typed before/after change capture produces minimal logical operations and an explicit conservative FullRebuild where precision is not yet supported;
- immutable mapping snapshots bind authority, applied revision, active scene, scene epoch, projection digest, mapping epoch, renderer/device identity and generation, actual generation-bearing renderer handles, and reverse lookup;
- stable ID, projection identity, and live renderer handle remain three distinct identity layers;
- publication prepares complete next registries before a no-throw swap; stale generations reject before renderer calls;
- scene selection/root preview use a distinct scene/view epoch rather than fabricating document revision.

`P5-10` tests cover exact single-field capture, transform descendant effects, visibility inheritance, material/variant final bindings, scene activation, Undo/Redo forward revisions, stale generation, mapping determinism, missing/reused slots, and candidate rollback.

`P5-20` implements the renderer transaction as a standalone module:

- `RendererTargetFence` binds backend, renderer instance, device instance/generation, mapping epoch, applied revision, scene epoch, and projection digest;
- `SceneApplyDisposition` distinguishes accepted incremental, accepted full rebuild, rejected, failed before submit, and failed after submit;
- `SceneApplyResult` returns typed error, applied fences, queue submission tokens, created/retired handles, counters, and optional fallback reason;
- `stageSceneGeneration`, `submitSceneGeneration`, `publishSceneGeneration() noexcept`, and `retireSceneGeneration` own unpublished resources and never mutate active registries during staging;
- descriptor generations and mapping become visible only after upload dependencies are established;
- pre-submit cleanup is immediate; submitted orphans retire by exact queue tokens; no device-wide idle is used for rollback.

Required counters include received/accepted/rejected by reason, operations/coalesced, logical work by class, exact geometry/texture/other uploaded bytes and ranges, resources created/logically retired/physically destroyed, retirement backlog, rebuild reason buckets, rollback/failure/publication/partial-publication, device idle by reason, and current fences. Rejected/rolled-back work cannot appear applied.

`P5-20` fault tests inject validation, CPU allocation, RHI allocation, descriptor staging, recording, each submission, prepublish, and retirement enqueue. They assert old active generation/fences/digest exact, no discoverable staged handles, correct orphan retirement, zero partial publication, and zero device idle.

`P5-90` integrates without weakening the frozen modules. Initial operation policy is:

| Operation | Required P5 result |
|---|---|
| node transform, visibility, material scalar/binding/variant, camera, light | incremental, exact minimal ranges, zero geometry/texture bytes unless the operation itself replaces those resources |
| instance add/remove | incremental only after atomic registry/mapping publication is proven; otherwise reason-coded structural rebuild |
| hierarchy add/delete/reparent, split/merge, schema changes | reason-coded transactional full snapshot initially |
| scene switch, global Merge, Compact | reason-coded transactional full snapshot |
| stale/gap/mapping/scene/device mismatch | reject with zero RHI side effects and request a separately validated snapshot; never silently rebuild from the stale delta |

P5 integration tests run pure CPU suites, fake-RHI transaction suites, direct executables, Debug/Release public contracts, Vulkan validation/sync validation for incremental and generation swap, D3D12 object contracts, Metal capability rejection before mutation, Android surface loss/zero extent lifecycle, and dependency/RHI scans. Accepted incremental transactions must have `partialPublicationCount=0`, `fullRebuildCount=0`, `geometryBytesUploaded=0`, `textureBytesUploaded=0`, and `deviceIdleCalls=0` for transform/material/light/visibility parameter edits.

`G5` independently rebinds all P5 paths and reruns the same gates from a fresh contained build/evidence root. It inspects hidden idle calls, old-resource overwrite, descriptor aliasing, false counters, stale-handle binding, incomplete world/bounds/light propagation, candidate publication, Android lifecycle, configured target closure, and all failure points. Gate P5 PASS requires all P5 tests/evidence and zero forbidden dependency/native finding; otherwise the verdict is FAIL/BLOCKED.

### 7.2 P6 contracts

`P6-00` freezes one selection authority and the shared immutable viewport contract before either picking or Gizmo/Grid work starts:

- `SceneSelectionValue` contains none, Node, Primitive occurrence, Mesh, Material, Camera, or Light using authority/generation-safe IDs;
- identical set and clearing empty are idempotent; same-Primitive viewport toggle is an explicit controller action, not a non-idempotent setter;
- every accepted change increments one selection revision and emits one ordered end-of-frame event, including clear and mutation reconciliation;
- explicit stable-ID remap is used when supplied; otherwise stale/deleted selection clears with no vector-index fallback;
- hidden live selection remains inspectable but derives no highlight and cannot be newly picked;
- browser reveal/scroll never forces a tab change;
- clipboard codec emits exact `gltf_material:<unsigned document index>`, parses complete ASCII decimal with checked overflow, accepts leading zero input but never emits it, revalidates against the active document on click, preserves enabled-but-invalid canonical out-of-range behavior, and remains non-history.
- `EditorViewportMetrics` is a backend-neutral immutable value containing the logical half-open viewport rectangle, physical attachment extent, framebuffer scale/DPI inputs, viewport generation, and projection/view identity needed for one checked logical-to-physical conversion and projection-aware constant logical-pixel sizing; it exposes no ImGui, RHI, or native backend type.

`P6-10` freezes render occurrence and asynchronous pick contracts:

- `PrimitiveOccurrenceKey { scene, node, primitive, instanceOrdinal }` distinguishes one definition reused by several nodes/instances;
- immutable one-to-many occurrence snapshots map a generation-bearing `RenderOccurrenceId` to that key and visibility; framebuffer tokens index only the retained snapshot;
- `EditorSceneFence` binds authority, document revision, projection revision, scene, scene epoch, and device generation;
- `EditorPickFence` adds viewport generation and view revision;
- requests carry serial, intent, sample, and world ray; results always terminate as hit/miss/error/cancelled and may complete out of order;
- the controller commits terminal results in request serial order; cancellation releases head-of-line;
- stale full fence is a no-effect discard; current-fence invalid/hidden/unknown/non-finite/non-positive single is blank/clear, while the same double is a no-op;
- Node highlight expands visible subtree occurrences in document order; Primitive highlights exactly its occurrence.

`P6-20` consumes the completed `P6-10` `EditorPickingTypes`/terminal-result contract and the `P6-00` `EditorViewportMetrics` contract read-only, then implements the strict delayed classifier and single-owner router:

- states are IDLE, SINGLE_PENDING, DOUBLE, and DRAG;
- first release waits; strict `elapsed > ImGui MouseDoubleClickTime` emits single at the then-current pointer/viewport; a recognized second press emits exactly one double with no preceding single; drag emits neither;
- document/scene/viewport destruction resets pending physical intent;
- input priority is modal/dialog, active or latched Gizmo, ImGui captured widget/text, eligible viewport picking, camera;
- logical-to-pixel conversion uses the immutable half-open viewport rectangle and actual attachment extent with no double DPI multiplication;
- camera double hit uses finite `origin + direction * distance`, navigation speed equals positive distance, keeps eye, updates one view revision; miss/stale changes neither selection nor camera.

P6 focused tests include six selection kinds, event/revision exactness, authority/generation reuse, same primitive definition on two occurrences, classifier `T-epsilon/T/T+epsilon`, drag/takeover, all clipboard partitions and document switches, viewport edges at 100/125/150/200 percent DPI, out-of-order pick completion, every fence mismatch, occurrence deletion/hide/reuse, camera modeled `[1,2,-2]`/`5`, browser focus, and highlight fence handoff.

`P6-90` wires projection occurrence metadata, upload planning, asynchronous readback, highlight, clipboard adapter, camera/focus adapters, and app input ordering through `RendererFacade`. No normal pick blocks or waits for idle. Device/projection replacement cancels old requests safely. Android excludes desktop picking/highlight orchestration while shared public contracts remain neutral.

Gate P6 requires all entry points to observe one selection revision; exactly one terminal completion per accepted request; no stale alias; delayed single/double exactness; camera/focus/clipboard/highlight/UI agreement; high-DPI and resize correctness; one-owner input; zero forbidden dependency/native finding; and an `X-O06`-consistent Escape/release oracle. Missing visual/runtime evidence is BLOCKED, not a partial PASS.

